  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EngenderHealth SRHR (Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights) Burkina Faso - Engenderhealth SRHR Burkina Faso</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">EngenderHealth SRHR (Sexuell och reproduktiv h&#xe4;lsa och r&#xe4;ttigheter) Burkina Faso</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EngenderHealth, project aims to expand access to quality abortion care and reduce unintended pregnancies among vulnerable populations and in humanitarian settings in Burkina Faso.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">EngenderHealth, projektet syftar till att &#xf6;ka tillg&#xe5;ngen till kvalitativ abortv&#xe5;rd och minska antalet oavsiktliga graviditeter bland utsatta befolkningsgrupper och i humanit&#xe4;ra situationer i Burkina Faso.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to reduce maternal morbidity and mortality associated with unsafe abortion and increase the ability of women, including adolescent girls and young women, particularly those who are internally displaced and living in host communities, to realize their bodily autonomy.
 This will be done through four mutually reinforcing objectives: 
1.Create a sustainable advocacy environment and a strong movement for quality safe abortion and sexual and reproductive health (SRH)
2.Improve the policy, legal, and strategic environment to advance quality abortion care
3.Increase the agency of women and adolescents to prevent unintended pregnancies and access quality abortion care 
4.Improve availability of quality, integrated comprehensive abortion care (CAC), family planning (FP), and gender-based violence (GBV) services for underserved and displaced populations</narrative>
  </description>
